I'm locking this thread subject, which means that people can start new =
threads, but messages will be held if it replies to this one.

spt
(for the chairs)

> On Oct 16, 2026, at 01:49, IETF Chair <chair@ietf.org> wrote:
>=20
> # Last Call Result
>=20
> The IESG received feedback from the community in response to the IETF =
Last Call on the proposed RFC 3683 PR-action for Ken Kubota [1]. After =
evaluating this feedback, the IESG has concluded there is rough =
consensus to proceed with the PR-action.
>=20
> Per the terms described in Section 2 of RFC 3683, the administrators =
of the ietf, tls, sshm, and mod-discuss lists are directed to suspend =
Ken Kubota=E2=80=99s posting privileges.  Additionally, this same =
section advises =E2=80=9Cmaintainers of any IETF mailing list may, at =
their discretion, also remove posting rights to that IETF mailing =
list.=E2=80=9D
>=20
> # Highlights from the Community Feedback
>=20
> The IESG thanks the community for providing this feedback and =
highlights the following feedback.
>=20
> ## Additional Justification for Action
>=20
> In addition to the messages outlined in [1], the following additional =
message was requested during the IETF Last Call to be added to the =
record motivating this PR action by the community:
>=20
> * =
https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ietf/OrvxKgjrEOMb95KAWoJYSilDxiY/
>=20
> ## Recommendations for PR actions
>=20
> The community made the following recommendations regarding PR actions:
>=20
> * Ensuring that the subject of the PR action is directly notified in =
addition to using the last-call@ietf.org mailing list.
>=20
> * Harmonizing active PR actions with the new RFC 9945-defined =
procedures.
>=20
> ## Implementing RFC9945
>=20
> The community expressed an urgency to fully implement the procedures =
of RFC 9945.
>=20
> # Conclusion
>=20
> The IESG reiterates that the purpose of this action is to minimize =
disruptive behavior by a single participant.  The IESG also reaffirms =
that a diverse set of opinions in the standards process is both =
important for the IETF and actively encouraged.
>=20
> Per RFC 9945, the IETF Moderator Team [2] is authoring the first draft =
of the new moderation procedures.  For discussion about IETF moderation =
procedures use mod-discuss@ietf.org [3].
>=20
> Roman Danyliw
> (as IETF Chair, for the IESG)
>=20
> [1] =
https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/last-call/JZXmLcVXUPtYWfMC2MMpPVOsTN=
M/
> [2] https://datatracker.ietf.org/group/ietfmoderators/about/
> [3] =
https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ietf-announce/kVletyOqMHSiXpsLAeqaB4=
CPsdQ/
> _______________________________________________
> ietf mailing list -- ietf@ietf.org
> To unsubscribe send an email to ietf-leave@ietf.org


